    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "The \"until the end of your opponent's turn, this Digimon isn't affected by the effects of their Digimon\" part activates even if not DNA digivolving.  The \"place 1 of your opponent's Digimon with as high or lower a level as the number of cards in your or their security stack at the bottom of their security stack\" part only activates if DNA digivolving.",
        "question": "Does this card’s [When Digivolving] effect activate when performing a non-DNA digivolution?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, this effect places 1 of your opponent's Digimon with as high or lower a level as the number of cards in either your or their security stack at the bottom of their security stack, not the total number of cards.",
        "question": "Does this card’s [When Digivolving] effect place 1 of my opponent's Digimon with as high or lower a level as the total number of cards in my or their security stack at the bottom of their security stack?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No, you can't.  If your opponent has a Digimon with as high or lower a level than the number of either your or your opponent's security cards, you must place those Digimon at the bottom of their security stack for this card's [When Digivolving] effect.",
        "question": "I have 5 security cards, and my opponent has 1 security card.  Can I refer to the number of my opponent's security cards for this card's [When Digivolving] effect so I don't place their Digimon at the bottom of the security stack?",
        "reference": "[2]"
      }
    ]
